Current kernel helpers being used

Channel tagging idea

We introduced two waiting modes without adding fields to struct proc:

#define CO_CHAN_SCHED(p)  ((void *)(p))
#define CO_CHAN_DIRECT(p) ((void *)(((uint64)(p)) | 1ULL))

Purpose:
	•	CO_CHAN_SCHED(p) = process is waiting via the scheduler-based path (co_sleep)
	•	CO_CHAN_DIRECT(p) = process is waiting via the direct-switch path

Current helper functions
	•	find_proc_by_pid(pid) returns target with target->lock held
	•	is_co_waiting(p) checks whether process is sleeping on either coroutine channel
	•	is_co_waiting_sched(p) checks scheduler-wait path only
	•	co_sleep(p) does scheduler-based sleep:
	•	acquire p->lock
	•	set chan
	•	set state=SLEEPING
	•	call sched()
	•	clear chan
	•	release p->lock

Current direct-switch implementation idea

In sys_co_yield:
	•	if target is not waiting:
	•	release target->lock
	•	call co_sleep(curr)
	•	return when resumed
	•	if target is waiting:
	•	put value into target->trapframe->a0
	•	put current process into sleeping state on direct channel
	•	set target to RUNNING
	•	set mycpu()->proc = target
	•	do swtch(&curr->context, &target->context)

Main problem observed

The direct handoff mostly works, but later the kernel crashes with:
